# W - Ugur interatomic potential, CANDIDATE, re-cut, switched
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * W_recut.ugur W
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD.  CANDIDATE, not part of the published library.  Against measured neutron dispersion this arm reaches 8.3 % over the 16 elements that have both a candidate record and a neutron curve and were not rejected outright, against 11.2 % for the published switched arm on the same 16.  That gap is almost all alkali: sodium, potassium, rubidium and caesium are where the arm gains most and are also what it breaks warm.  Leave them out and it is 8.3 % against 8.9 % over 11 elements, better in 7 - a wash.  There is no measured reason to prefer this arm for its dispersion
# MD: structure screened - holds its shape at 600 K (299 K, as equipartition requires).  This tested the SHAPE, not energy conservation; for that see the truncation line above.
#
# LATTICE STABILITY: this set is NOT a harmonic minimum.
# Along the Setyawan-Curtarolo path its frequencies reach -10.903 cm^-1,
# with 0.23 % of the sampled modes imaginary.  That is a separate
# failure from the 600 K screen above and is not covered by it.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Measured dispersion: 17.2 % against 17.8 % for the published switched
# arm - better.
# On the 41 accepted candidate records the re-cut is close to break-even
# overall: thermal expansion 30.7 % -> 25.6 % median, 10 better and 10
# worse; 300 K elastic constants 3.4 % -> 2.7 %, 7 better and 3 worse.
#
# REJECTED: this record did NOT pass selection -
# it carries a mode at -10.9 cm^-1 on the symmetry path; it puts fcc lowest, 424 meV/atom below bcc.
# It is kept as the control the accepted records are read against,
# not as a potential.  Do not use it.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of W at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
